Fail on a CRC error in a bzip2 stream with no data.
After a stream holding no blocks, the status is still RETVAL_OK when
the stream CRC is checked. A mismatch printed "CRC error" but then broke
out of the loop with that status, so unpack_bz2_stream() returned
success: bunzip2 exited 0 and deleted the input. Return a data error.

---
 archival/libarchive/decompress_bunzip2.c |    1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

--- a/archival/libarchive/decompress_bunzip2.c
+++ b/archival/libarchive/decompress_bunzip2.c
@@ -817,6 +817,7 @@
 		}
 		if (bd->headerCRC != bd->totalCRC) {
 			bb_simple_error_msg("CRC error");
+			i = RETVAL_DATA_ERROR; /* i may be RETVAL_OK here */
 			break;
 		}
 
